# Effective collision strengths for the h20 (n-resolved) H I macro-atom Lyman lines.
# Source: CHIANTI h_1 (Anderson et al. 2000, J. Phys. B 33, 1255; revised 2002).  All (l, J)
# components 1s -> n'l_j are summed (h20 levels are n-resolved) and re-sampled at the 13
# Burgess & Tully (1992) nodes of the listed type and C, with the reduced temperature
# defined by the h20 transition energy.  The line data match h20_lines.dat exactly.
# CHIANTI h_1 has no 2p -> n data, so no Balmer records are given (Balmer lines keep the
# default approximation).  Accuracy of each record (as Sirocco evaluates it) vs CHIANTI:
# Ly alpha  n=1-2   3 CHIANTI components  BT type 1 C=1.7   Ups(1e4 K)=0.752  max |dUps/Ups| (1e3-1e6 K) = 0.8%
# Ly beta   n=1-3   5 CHIANTI components  BT type 1 C=1.6   Ups(1e4 K)=0.253  max |dUps/Ups| (1e3-1e6 K) = 0.4%
# Ly gamma  n=1-4   7 CHIANTI components  BT type 1 C=1.6   Ups(1e4 K)=0.114  max |dUps/Ups| (1e3-1e6 K) = 0.4%
# Ly delta  n=1-5   9 CHIANTI components  BT type 1 C=1.5   Ups(1e4 K)=0.081  max |dUps/Ups| (1e3-1e6 K) = 1.0%
# Each CSTREN record must be immediately followed by its SCT and SCUPS lines.
